Subject: Reject malformed UTF-8 hostnames before IDNA conversion

Origin: DHI-internal (Go 1.26 compatibility)
Description: Go 1.26 passes malformed byte sequences through IDNA conversion, so validate hostnames before origin comparison.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/Azure/azure-service-operator.git 03b1e9142cdff81c573f2d3492dc4c5e1817cd2e path=v2
Verify: cmd `go test ./internal/httpclient -run '^TestOrigin_InvalidIDNA$' -count=1` expect "PASS"
Forwarded: no (the release test already specifies the required behavior)
Drop-When: never: origin validation must reject malformed UTF-8 on every supported Go runtime

Go 1.26 accepts a malformed byte sequence during IDNA lookup despite the release test requiring rejection. Validate the hostname encoding explicitly so request-origin checks keep the intended boundary.

diff --git a/v2/internal/httpclient/origin.go b/v2/internal/httpclient/origin.go
index 780a438c..7de476f0 100644
--- a/v2/internal/httpclient/origin.go
+++ b/v2/internal/httpclient/origin.go
@@ -86 +86 @@ func originOf(u *url.URL) (Origin, bool) {
-	if host == "" || strings.ContainsAny(host, "%\\/?#@ \t\r\n") {
+	if host == "" || !utf8.ValidString(host) || strings.ContainsAny(host, "%\\/?#@ \t\r\n") {
